([00:00:05] Daniel Okafor: Last time you planned to let your leads run the Monday stand-) Tj T*
(up. How did that go?) Tj T*
([00:00:22] Amara Okoro: I let them run it twice. The second time I stepped back in when) Tj T*
(the shipping delays came up.) Tj T*
([00:01:34] Daniel Okafor: What made you step back in?) Tj T*
([00:01:50] Amara Okoro: I wanted the decision made in the room. Kai had a plan for the) Tj T*
(Harbor contract deliveries, I just didn't wait for it.) Tj T*
([00:02:44] Daniel Okafor: What would waiting have looked like?) Tj T*
([00:03:02] Amara Okoro: Asking Kai what he'd do, and then saying nothing for a minute.) Tj T*
([00:05:10] Daniel Okafor: You said last time you'd let your lead make the weekly call.) Tj T*
(What happened with that?) Tj T*
([00:05:31] Amara Okoro: I did it once. Kai made the call on the weekend rota and it) Tj T*
(worked fine. Honestly better than mine.) Tj T*
([00:06:15] Daniel Okafor: What did you notice when it worked?) Tj T*
([00:06:40] Amara Okoro: I think I hold on because I worry it reflects on me if it goes) Tj T*
(wrong. But the rota was better because Kai knows the drivers.) Tj T*
([00:24:10] Daniel Okafor: What will you try before we meet again?) Tj T*
([00:24:25] Amara Okoro: At Monday's stand-up, when a problem comes up, I'll ask the lead) Tj T*
(who owns it for their plan before I say anything.) Tj T*
([00:25:05] Amara Okoro: And maybe hand Kai the rota for the whole month. I need to think) Tj T*
(about that one.) Tj T*
([00:25:40] Daniel Okafor: Let's capture both, and you can tell me next time whether the) Tj T*
(rota one is right for you.) Tj T*
